      "text": "Given $150^\\circ = 180^\\circ - 30^\\circ$, we can use the cosine difference formula:\n\\[\n\\cos(180^\\circ - \\theta) = -\\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\nSubstituting $\\theta = 30^\\circ$, we get:\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = -\\cos 30^\\circ\n\\]\nSince $\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, it follows that:\n\\[\n\\cos 150^\\circ = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\]\nSo, $\\cos 150^\\circ = \\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}$.\nTherefore, the answer is \\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}.",
